<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14668" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dŏlŏpes</span></b> , um
			(<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>sing.
			acc.</i> Dolopem, <i><span class="en">Liv. 42, 58</span></i>), m., =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δόλοπες</span>, <i>the
				Dolopes</i> or <i>Dolopians</i>, <i>a people in Thessaly</i>, <i>renowned in
			fable</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 2, 3, § 6</span></i> (who
			reckons them among the Aetolians); <i><span class="en">Cic. Rep. 2,
				4, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 2, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
				364</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep. Cim. 2,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dŏlŏpēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of the
				Dolopes</i>, <i>Dolopian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">busta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 2, 10</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dŏlŏpēis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., adj.,
				<i>Dolopian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbs,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Ctimene</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hyg.
					Fab. 14</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dŏlŏpĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>the part of
				Thessaly formerly inhabited by the Dolopes</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 32,
				13 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
